  "notes": "{違|ちが}う means to differ or to be wrong—a very common verb with two distinct uses.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- No standard transitive pair\n- Pattern: {違|ちが}う\n\nSENSE 1 - DIFFERENT:\n- X⟦と→と：00512_to⟧Y⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{違|ちが}う: X and Y are different\n- X⟦と→と：00512_to⟧{違|ちが}って: unlike X\n- ⟦{全然|ぜんぜん}→全然：00598_zenzen⟧{違|ちが}う: completely different\n\nSENSE 2 - WRONG/INCORRECT:\n- ⟦{答|こた}え→答え：00790_kotae⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{違|ちが}う: the answer is wrong\n- {違|ちが}います: No, that's not right (polite denial)\n- ⟦ちょっと→ちょっと：00595_chotto⟧{違|ちが}う: a bit wrong/off\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{違|ちが}い→違い：03432_chigai⟧: difference (noun)\n- ⟦{間違|まちが}い→間違い：03733_machigai⟧: mistake\n- ⟦{間違|まちが}える→間違える：01109_machigaeru⟧: to make a mistake\n- ⟦{異|こと}なる→異なる：02101_kotonaru⟧: to differ (formal)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {違|ちが}っている: is different, is wrong (stative — describes a current state, not an ongoing action)\n- Note: {違|ちが}う is one of a small group of stative verbs (along with ⟦{優|すぐ}れる→優れる：02119_sugureru⟧, ⟦{似|に}る→似る：01159_niru⟧, ⟦そびえる→そびえる：10360_sobieru⟧) that describe inherent states. Both plain {違|ちが}う and {違|ちが}っている are used to express the stative meaning; {違|ちが}っている often highlights that a specific item deviates from a norm or expectation. ⟦{電話番号|でんわばんごう}→電話番号：10159_denwabangou⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{違|ちが}っています = 'the phone number is wrong (compared to what it should be).' The plain {違|ちが}います is the standard polite denial 'no, that's not right.'",
